 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "직업 어휘와 현재완료·현재형으로 일 설명하기",
   "en": "talking about jobs: present simple, present perfect and who"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "직업은 'I'm a + 직업'이나 'I work for / at + 장소'로 말합니다. 얼마 동안 일했는지는 현재완료와 for를 씁니다 (I have worked here for five years). 하는 일은 who / that으로 설명할 수 있습니다 (a nurse who looks after patients).",
   "en": "Say your job with 'I'm a + job' or 'I work for / at + place'. Say how long with the present perfect and for (I have worked here for five years). Describe what someone does with who / that (a nurse who looks after patients)."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "직업 / job",
     "I'm a nurse. I work at a hospital."
    ],
    [
     "기간 / how long",
     "I have worked here for five years."
    ],
    [
     "하는 일 / who",
     "He is an engineer who repairs computers."
    ],
    [
     "지원 / applying",
     "I applied for the job."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "직업 앞에는 a / an: I'm a nurse.",
    "en": "Use a / an before a job: I'm a nurse."
   },
   {
    "ko": "work for + 회사, work at + 장소.",
    "en": "work for + company; work at + place."
   },
   {
    "ko": "지원: apply for a job.",
    "en": "apply for a job."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
